{"learned": "We have six sources about ARRI's professional focus, its smartphone partnership with HONOR, and the fact that creators currently use ARRI gear rented rather than owned. No source provides direct evidence of individual creators\u2019 willingness to pay for a new ARRI product or demand for a differentiated consumer offering. The existing evidence supports the idea that ARRI is perceived as a professional standard but does not confirm purchase intent or price sensitivity. Two open theories (T1 and T2) attribute adoption to brand prestige and premium pricing; a third theory (T3) will attribute adoption to affordable entry\u2011level hardware combined with smartphone integration. A test can compare a high\u2011",
"uncertain": "The key uncertainty is whether individual creators will actually buy ARRI products at premium prices or if they would only adopt if ARRI offers lower\u2011cost, integrated solutions. The current evidence does not resolve this.",
"why_next": "A low\u2011cost, smartphone\u2011integrated concept test can separate the mechanisms: premium\u2011focused theories predict stronger interest in a high\u2011price professional offering, while the affordability theory predicts stronger interest in a lower\u2011price kit that leverages the existing smartphone partnership. The test fits the \u20ac20k budget and 12\u2011week window.",
"call": {"name": "add_theory", "arguments": {"claim": "Individual creators will adopt ARRI products if ARRI offers affordable entry\u2011level hardware that integrates with the smartphone partnership, providing professional\u2011grade capabilities at a lower price point.", "who_benefits": "ARRI gains volume sales and a new consumer base by capturing creators who need professional image quality but cannot afford premium cinema cameras.", "why_behaviour_changes": "Creators are price\u2011sensitive; a lower\u2011cost kit that works with their existing smartphone reduces the barrier to ownership and complements the HONOR partnership.", "how_value_is_captured": "ARRI can sell a bundled camera accessory and software subscription at a consumer price, generating recurring revenue and cross\u2011selling opportunities.", "assumptions": ["There is a market of individual creators willing to purchase hardware priced below \u20ac500.", "The smartphone partnership already delivers professional\u2011grade image quality that can be enhanced with a simple accessory.", "Creators value seamless integration between capture and post\u2011production tools."], "predictions": ["If ARRI offers a sub\u2011\u20ac500 kit that integrates with the HONOR phone, the intention to purchase will be higher than for a stand\u2011alone premium camera priced above \u20ac5,000.", "Willingness to pay for the affordable kit will be at least \u20ac200, indicating sufficient demand.", "Creators using the kit will report higher perceived value than those offered only the premium camera."]}}
